# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sched-2 window (the admission levers; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sched-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-2 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-sched-2/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the
# same in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone.
# L1 (TIMED, the ARM of the first ABAB pair): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-sch-s5-all, the ship-5 candidate with the gate marker in place of its owner
# waiver id and the three levers on (QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_SEED_FIRST=1, QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_HOLD_REUSE=1, QWEN_FAST_ADMISSION_LEDGER_TRIM=1), the same tests as C1, on Swift.
# ESTIMATE (docs/tp4-sched2.md section 5, arithmetic over the control run's own segments): concurrent8_steady's last first token 15.4 s -> about 12.7 s (-17%; the ledger
# trim 1.7 s, the hold reuse 0.6 s, the seed first 0.35 s), up to 11.8 s if the owed decode rounds shrink with the step; a returning turn's first token p50 1.46 s -> about
# 1.12 s (-23%: the seed first 275 ms, the hold reuse 63 ms). The decoders' tokens a second and agent_turns' committed rate must NOT fall. READ: c2_smoke_check clean; the
# lines each lever logs (a lever whose line is absent did not engage, and its arm reads NOT_EXERCISED): "[PINDIAG] admission pipeline installed: seed_first=.. hold_reuse=..
# ledger_trim=.." once; SEED FIRST: "[PINDIAG] admission seed first deferred request=.. slot=.." and "[PINDIAG] admission seed first built request=.. ms=..
# after_seed_ms=.." per deferred admission (ms is the bind the first token did not wait for; after_seed_ms is how long the token had been out when the bind began),
# "[PINDIAG] admission seed first eager request=.. reason=.." for each bind that stayed in the sampler; HOLD REUSE: "[PINDIAG] admission hold reading reused prompt=..
# age_ms=.. reuses=.." per reused hold (the dram admission fit lines then number the real readings); LEDGER TRIM: "[PINDIAG] admission ledger trim: the memory ledger ended
# after the attach" once and no "memory_ledger_before" line with "op": "rebind" in the whole log; EXACT READ: every user's answer is byte-identical to the control's (the
# same checkpoint, greedy: a difference is a token a lever changed and is NO-GO); no "audit mismatch", no "fell back", no "admission seed first: the bind of" error line (a
# refusal after a seed had gone: it stops the engine, and the preflight makes it unexpected), no engine death, no stall. Then, after the four boots (C1 L1 C2 L2): per user
# the first-token time, paired by index against the two controls and the control-to-control floor, for concurrent8_steady (the eight arrivals in arrival order) and
# agent_turns (python3 scripts/ci/agent_turns.py report <smoke> <container> on each leg); the decoders' rate and the longest gap between two tokens of a stream (a lever
# that only moves delay shows here). RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED: the ARC runner sets are at ZERO for this job (ORDER, ARC-ZERO); no build, no CI push, no other job beside it.
# READ the arm with python3 scripts/ci/sched2_report.py <arm container log> --second <control container log> (and --burst for the first eight fresh prompts, one line an
# arrival): the serial chain (hold + drain + bind) of returning turns and of fresh prompts, the bind's parts (A, B, C and C's phases), the ledger bracket and the conv-slice
# readback (only at a slot's first use), the seed first lines (deferred, bound in the sampler and why, how long the first token left ahead of the bind), the hold reuse
# lines (how many holds took no allocator reading, their age). Every figure prints "-" when no line is behind it. The model of the same arithmetic is python3
# scripts/ci/sched2_model.py (ESTIMATES: docs/tp4-sched2.md section 5). CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds
# "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4 key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is
# not read or written)" once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound
# ..." line; the models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. Duration (estimate): 35 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sched-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-sch-s5-all
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,agent_turns
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=80
